  "source": [
    "App Store Connect API OpenAPI specification 4.5.1 (info.version \"4.5.1\"), offline snapshot docs/openapi/latest.json of github.com/rorkai/App-Store-Connect-CLI (MIT), last synced 2026-10-07; it mirrors Apple's download https://developer.apple.com/sample-code/app-store-connect/app-store-connect-openapi-specification.zip",
    "components.schemas: ScreenshotDisplayType, PreviewType, AppAssetLibraryPlacementType, AppAssetLibraryDisplayClass, AppAssetLibraryPlacementPlatform, AppAssetLibraryAssetCategory",
    "rorkai/App-Store-Connect-CLI internal/screenshotcatalog/catalog.go (APP_IPHONE_69 is a local alias the CLI sends as APP_IPHONE_67) and internal/cli/assets/assets_previews.go (IPHONE_69 → IPHONE_67)"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Every value below is a member of the named 4.5.1 enum. Which enum member belongs to which Vitrin target is the mapping Vitrin uses; for the classic types it follows the pixel sizes in Apple's screenshot specifications and fastlane/asc (6.9\" iPhone = APP_IPHONE_67 — the classic enum has no 69).",
    "screenshotDisplayType/previewType null = the classic appScreenshotSets/appPreviewSets API has no type for this target (iPhone Duo is not in ScreenshotDisplayType or PreviewType of 4.5.1); those go through the App Asset Library.",
    "Asset Library placements carry placementType + placementGroup. The placementGroup id is not an enum: it is resolved at run time from GET /v1/appAssetLibraryRefData placementProfileGroups[] by (platform, displayClassId). `vitrin doctor` checks every mapping below against refData.",
    "category: APP_SCREENSHOTS_AND_PREVIEWS for APP_SCREENSHOT/APP_PREVIEW, CREATIVE_ASSETS for header, search and event assets."
  ],
